Title: "Named Operators"
Id: "7857f35a-dfb7-4a59-903f-1f17d71e49d4"

Text: "Named operators use a name surrounded by bars.

```mlg-fragment
x |op| y
x :|op| y
x |op|: y
x :|op|: y
f| x
x |f
```

The colon-directed forms choose which operand type is used to resolve the operator. Prefix and postfix forms have the same arity as a one-argument function call.

A plain named operator is syntactic sugar for application: `x |op| y` means
`op(x, y)`, and `f| x` and `x |f` mean `f(x)`. The content between the bars may
be a dotted **member path** whose segments are names or operator symbols, such
as `|M.*|` or `|x.y.z|`; it tracks down through a value's fields, so `x |M.*| y`
is the member call `M.*(x, y)`.

```mlg-fragment
x |M.*| y
x |a.b.c| y
```"
Id: "0c505d0d-f3b3-4d15-b36c-740a147f4302"
